1
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,241
HPSEDC staff sign in with the Overseas Placement Cell account.

2
00:00:14,301 --> 00:00:23,679
In this version of HireStream, HPSEDC works as the single super agency: every vacancy belongs to this account, and every applicant comes to this team.

3
00:00:23,739 --> 00:00:31,733
The dashboard opens with the agency card, the verified badge, and the Applicant Pipeline, which counts applicants at each stage.

4
00:00:31,793 --> 00:00:35,320
Below it are the most recent jobs and recruitment drives.

5
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,970
The Post Job button is always at the top of the left menu.

6
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,094
To add a vacancy, click Post Job.

7
00:00:48,154 --> 00:00:55,261
Enter the job title and the overseas employer, then choose the destination country, the city and the job category.

8
00:00:55,321 --> 00:01:00,857
The category matters: it decides which trade documents a selected candidate is asked for.

9
00:01:00,917 --> 00:01:09,847
Set the monthly salary as a fixed amount in the local currency, the minimum experience, and optionally the qualification and language criteria.

10
00:01:09,907 --> 00:01:13,682
Add a description and the key skills, then click Publish Job.

11
00:01:13,742 --> 00:01:16,763
The vacancy is live for candidates straight away.

12
00:01:16,823 --> 00:01:19,970
Save as Draft keeps it private until you are ready.

13
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:37,982
My Jobs lists every vacancy, with filters for active, draft and closed jobs, a search box, and sorting by date or deadline.

14
00:02:38,042 --> 00:02:39,559
Open a job to manage it.

15
00:02:39,619 --> 00:02:49,087
From the job page you can edit it, preview it exactly as a candidate sees it, copy a share link, close it when the batch is filled, or reopen it.

16
00:02:49,147 --> 00:02:54,673
Export CSV downloads the applicant list, and the ZIP export includes their documents.

17
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:59,470
Further down are the job analytics and the applicants for this job alone.

18
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:14,326
The Applications Pipeline shows every application across all jobs on one page.

19
00:03:14,386 --> 00:03:23,103
HPSEDC runs the direct, four stage process: Submitted, Interview, Selected and Placed, with Rejected and Withdrawn kept separately.

20
00:03:23,163 --> 00:03:24,912
Click a stage to filter it.

21
00:03:24,972 --> 00:03:29,602
The Stale chip finds applications that have waited seven days or more.

22
00:03:29,662 --> 00:03:35,632
You can search by candidate, job, company or skill, and filter by country, company or job.

23
00:03:35,692 --> 00:03:43,740
Click View to open the candidate's full profile: their trades, education, experience, documents and pre-departure status.

24
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:56,474
HPSEDC interviews every applicant, so the next step for a new application is Schedule interview.

25
00:03:56,534 --> 00:04:01,013
Choose the date and time, whether it is in person or virtual, and the venue.

26
00:04:01,073 --> 00:04:04,119
For a virtual interview, a meeting link is required.

27
00:04:04,179 --> 00:04:08,838
Add the interviewer's name, and link it to a recruitment drive if there is one.

28
00:04:08,898 --> 00:04:13,736
Schedule and Notify Candidate saves the interview and tells the candidate at once.

29
00:04:13,796 --> 00:04:19,710
The application moves to the Interview stage, where you can see whether the candidate has confirmed.

30
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:45,431
Candidates can confirm, decline, or ask to move their interview.

31
00:04:45,491 --> 00:04:49,330
A request shows up as an orange Respond to reschedule button.

32
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:54,764
The dialog shows the current time, the candidate's reason and the time they proposed.

33
00:04:54,824 --> 00:04:59,686
You can accept the proposed time, set a different time, or keep the original.

34
00:04:59,746 --> 00:05:03,650
Whichever you choose, the candidate is notified automatically.

35
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,762
After the interview, click Outcome.

36
00:05:11,822 --> 00:05:14,591
Choose Pass and Select, or Fail and Reject.

37
00:05:14,651 --> 00:05:17,222
Add a rating out of five and your notes.

38
00:05:17,282 --> 00:05:20,380
Notes are required when a candidate is rejected.

39
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:29,591
When you select a candidate, HireStream moves them to Selected, creates their offer, and tells them which documents they now need to upload.

40
00:05:29,651 --> 00:05:33,670
Before selection, a candidate is never asked for any document.

41
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:51,230
Open a selected candidate to manage their departure.

42
00:05:51,290 --> 00:05:59,719
The Deployment Readiness panel lists what is still missing, such as the passport, police clearance, medical, visa, orientation and insurance.

43
00:05:59,779 --> 00:06:08,208
The Pre-Departure Compliance section records their emigration details under the Emigration Act, and every change is written to the audit log.

44
00:06:08,268 --> 00:06:12,302
Under Visa and passport assistance, set the visa status with a note.

45
00:06:12,362 --> 00:06:14,469
The candidate is notified each time.

46
00:06:14,529 --> 00:06:19,948
Under Appointment and travel, set the travel date and upload the signed appointment letter.

47
00:06:20,008 --> 00:06:24,463
The candidate can accept the offer only once this letter has been uploaded.

48
00:06:24,523 --> 00:06:26,329
Accepting it marks them Placed.

49
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:39,602
HPSEDC's duty of care continues after departure.

50
00:06:39,662 --> 00:06:45,039
For every placed worker there are thirty, sixty and ninety day welfare check-ins.

51
00:06:45,099 --> 00:06:51,282
Click Record, choose OK, Concerns, No response or Not applicable, add a short note, and save.

52
00:06:51,342 --> 00:06:55,780
Missed check-ins appear on the administrator's Welfare SLA monitor.

53
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:16,043
Candidates can message HPSEDC from their dashboard.

54
00:07:16,103 --> 00:07:20,474
These messages arrive under Messages, with an unread count in the menu.

55
00:07:20,534 --> 00:07:23,033
Open a thread, type a reply, and send it.

56
00:07:23,093 --> 00:07:26,653
Formal complaints are handled separately under Grievances.

57
00:07:26,713 --> 00:07:35,079
Problems with an application are routed to this team automatically, and each grievance moves from review, to action taken, to resolved.

58
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:00,530
Reports gives the cell its own management view.

59
00:08:00,590 --> 00:08:11,349
It shows jobs, applicants, placements and the conversion rate, then pipeline health, operations and service levels, including welfare check-ins due and compliance alerts.

60
00:08:11,409 --> 00:08:19,940
At the bottom is the HPSEDC compliance section, with orientation and insurance coverage, the ECR mix and the top destination countries.

